  <h2 style="margin-bottom:34px">Four passes, no shortcuts</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step"><b>01</b><h3>Sculpt</h3><p>The emblem is modelled at 12× scale, then reduced onto a steel hub. Every letter is drawn by hand.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><b>02</b><h3>Sink</h3><p>Hubs are pressed into annealed tool steel, hardened to 60 HRC and polished until the fields read like black glass.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><b>03</b><h3>Strike</h3><p>Three strikes at 180 tonnes with an anneal between passes — that's what pulls the relief up crisp instead of soft.</p></div>
    <div class="step"><b>04</b><h3>Finish</h3><p>Hand antiquing, a lathe-cut highlight, edge numbering, and a final inspection under raking light. Rejects go back to the melt.</p></div>
